    ],

    flowPortal: {
      ok: 'Approved by you',
      rev: 'Revision requested — this image only',
      wait: 'Still coming',
    },
    flowDeliverPortal: `From ${WINDOW_THRESHOLD} products it lands in a portal you approve image by image — approved, in revision and still coming, all at once, none of them waiting on the others.`,
    flowDeliverLink: 'Below that it arrives as a download link, with the same production and the same check behind it.',

    flowChannels: [
      { t: 'Shop listing' },
      { t: 'Feed post' },
      { t: 'Reel or story' },
      { t: 'Banner' },
      { t: 'Marketplace' },
    ],

    // FIVE DISCLOSURES IN ONE CAPTION, because this figure replaced five. Every
    // sentence here was load-bearing somewhere else: drawn-not-photographed
    // (FigFanOut), not-a-screenshot (FigApproval), each frame IS its ratio and
    // the high-resolution claim that used to be a card of its own (FigFormats).
    // The prices sentence is new and is the price of making the figure quote
    // real numbers at all.
    flowNote: `A diagram, not a screenshot. The front photo is a real client file; the other frames are drawn, because they are slots in the delivery and not results this shirt has produced. Each crop is genuinely the ratio it is labelled with. Delivered files are high-resolution and e-commerce-ready. Prices come from the published ladder, ${vatLabel('excl', 'en')}.`,

    gateLead: 'No date is printed until the calendar clears it.',
    gateBody: 'A reserved window is confirmed before you pay, never after. If the week you need cannot be held, you hear that — not an optimistic guess. It is the one promise on this site we would rather lose an order over than break.',
